                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61cc3878-b084-4cde-ad2f-e85f45e964dc",
                                                "sense_id": "4083c13e-e476-3892-9c7a-f67ddd3bff0d",
                                                "text": "Jamestown Township isn’t the first library to have its operations disrupted in this way. Libraries across the country have recently become a culture war battleground, facing an unprecedented number of book challenges and bans from conservative and far-right extremist groups opposed to the inclusion of LGBTQ+ authors, staff, and events. Last month, a public library in Iowa was forced to close temporarily after all full-time employees quit. The exodus came after months of complaints from conservative residents, who criticized the display of LGBTQ+ books and complained of gender non-conforming library workers \"cross-dressing.\""
